## Why This Is Asked
Tests that cover feature flags and per-tenant isolation are common in real-world SaaS apps. This checks practicalend-to-end approach, not just basic UI tests.

## Key Concepts
- Feature flags and environment configuration
- Test data isolation per tenant
- Mocking backend for deterministic results
- Handling flaky networks with bounded retries
- UI assertions for conditional flows

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: outline for Playwright tests with two tenants
async function testOnboardingFlag(tenantId, flagOn){
  await createTenant(tenantId);
  await setFlag(flagOn ? "on" : "off", tenantId);
  await page.goto(`/onboarding?tenant=${tenantId}`);
  // assertions based on flag state
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to support parallel execution without flag leakage?
- How would you verify that the flag state propagation is eventual across multiple services?

