- How would you simulate varying network latency?
- How would you validate changing merge policies for A/B tests?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests for canary flag rollouts across a polyglot stack are critical to catching cross‑layer regressions and outage scenarios before full rollout.

## Key Concepts
- Feature flags across services and UI
- Canary routing and rollback triggers
- Fault injection (service down, latency) and observability
- End-to-end data integrity across components

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example Playwright test sketch (pseudo)
const { test, expect } = require('@playwright/test');

test('canary feature exposure aligns with flag', async ({ page }) => {
  // control exposure
  await page.route('**/flag-service/**', route => {
    route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ flag: 'newFeature', value: 10 }) });
  });
  await page.goto('https://app.example.com/');
  // verify UI reflects feature for canary users
  // verify backend calls include feature header, etc.
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure rollback latency and automate deactivation of the canary?
- How do you ensure idempotent backend mutations during rollback?

## Why This Is Asked
